Kam Kreiser 2026-09-14T08:08:56+10:00
KS-577: the two register-connector descriptions now say what a rotate does — corrected at their source and regenerated

Peter's one condition on PR #880 (review 5153311061): two `secuura-api.yaml` descriptions became false the moment revoke-on-rotate lands — "The old key stays active until explicitly revoked." and "`rotate: true` mints a replacement (revoke the old key separately)." — and this is the document Platform S reads.

Both live in `services/tenant-provisioning/src/tenant-provisioning.openapi.ts` (the yaml is generated from it): the `rotate` field description (`RegisterConnectorRequestSchema.rotate`) and the `register-connector` operation description. Rewritten from the code at this head — `revokePriorConnectorKeys` in `services/security/src/index.ts` retires every prior ACTIVE key of the same connector in the same tenant as part of the mint: `is_active = false` at once when `API_KEY_ROTATION_GRACE_SECONDS` is unset or 0, otherwise `expires_at` is clamped to now + that window. The env name is spelled as `index.ts` spells it. Nothing narrates a failure mode into the contract, and the text names only what the register-connector caller can observe (the gateway consumes `priorKeysRevoked` and returns `rotated`).

The yaml was REGENERATED (`npm run generate-openapi`), never hand-edited. Measured in order: `generate-openapi -- --check` PASS on the merged tree before the edit; after the .ts edit and before the regen, `--check` FAIL rc 1 ("generated YAML differs from on-disk version") — the control that a published sentence is checked by regenerating; after the regen, `git status` = exactly these two files and `git diff -U0` on the yaml = exactly 2 hunks, one at each description, no other path, schema or example; `npm run check:openapi` PASS (both halves: the byte compare and check-spec-examples, 405 example blocks).

Suites at this head (offline; bash 3.2.57, node v24.7.0, darwin arm64): services/security 15 files 195/195 (the ks577 file 8/8) · services/api-gateway 34 files 343/343 · services/tenant-provisioning 3 files 13/13 · tsc --noEmit clean in all three.

Not built this round, on the ticket for Kam's line as Peter asked: his items 3–5 (SQL-statement cells on the ks869 pattern; route cells on the ks742 harness; the zero-revoked warning/backfill; the validate-path cell). The merge of this PR is Kam's: it picks a cutover shape for Platform S.

